# Mas Oller: Tuesday vs. Wednesday, Restaurants and Transportation

**For your stay at Hotel Mas Pastora, Llafranc** ([📍 Map](https://www.google.com/maps/search/Hotel%20Mas%20Pastora%2C%20Llafranc%2C%20Spain))  
**Dates considered: Tuesday, September 8 and Wednesday, September 9, 2026**  
**Availability checked: August 26, 2026**

## Executive recommendation

**Tuesday remains the stronger winery day if you value the experience itself.** It is the only date with the English guided tour, at **11:00 a.m.**, and several good nearby restaurants are open afterward. The original recommendation of La Sala de l’Isaac for Tuesday was incorrect: its live reservation calendar marks Tuesday closed. Replace it with **El Pedró in Pals**, **Can Nau in Peratallada**, or **El Mas at Mas de Torrent**.[1] [2]

**Wednesday is the stronger food-and-wine day if you are comfortable doing the tasting without the tour.** Book lunch first at **La Sala de l’Isaac, Vicus or Candelaria**, spend some time in Pals or Peratallada, and then take the **5:00 p.m. tasting**. The 1:30 p.m. tasting conflicts with normal local lunch hours and is therefore less attractive.[1]

> **Best overall plan:** Tuesday 11:00 guided tour → 1:15 lunch at El Pedró → walk around medieval Pals ([📍 Map](https://www.google.com/maps/search/Pals%2C%20Girona%2C%20Spain)) → pre-booked car back to Mas Pastora.

