### 1. El Pedró: best Tuesday choice

> [📍 Map](https://www.google.com/maps/search/El%20Pedr%C3%B3%2C%20Pals%2C%20Girona%2C%20Spain) · 🚗 21 min from Mas Pastora · 7 min from Mas Oller

El Pedró is open for lunch on both Tuesday and Wednesday in September. It serves homemade Mediterranean cooking and rice from Pals inside the medieval village.[3] A 1:15 reservation after the Tuesday tour allows enough time for the short transfer and gives you the afternoon to wander Pals before returning to Llafranc.

This is the most balanced pairing for your preferences: good regional food, an attractive historic setting and no need to turn lunch into another elaborate tasting-menu event.

### 2. Can Nau: best casual Tuesday alternative

> [📍 Map](https://www.google.com/maps/search/Can%20Nau%2C%20Peratallada%2C%20Spain) · 🚗 26 min from Mas Pastora · 11 min from Mas Oller

Can Nau is open Tuesday and closed Wednesday. It specializes in traditional Empordà cooking, seasonal dishes and Pals rice in an 18th-century rural house with a summer terrace.[4] [5]

Choose this over El Pedró if you prefer **Peratallada** to Pals and want a less polished, more home-style lunch. Because its opening hours come from a current local listing rather than a live restaurant booking calendar, confirm by phone before building the afternoon around it: **+34 972 63 40 35**.

### 3. El Mas at Mas de Torrent: most reliable polished option

> [📍 Map](https://www.google.com/maps/search/El%20Mas%2C%20Mas%20de%20Torrent%2C%20Torrent%2C%20Girona%2C%20Spain) · 🚗 19 min from Mas Pastora · 3 min from Mas Oller

El Mas is open for lunch on both dates and sits only three minutes from the winery. It serves contemporary Catalan cooking with Empordà views and is the easiest logistical pairing.[6] It will feel more like a luxury-hotel meal than an impromptu village lunch, but it solves any Tuesday/Wednesday closure concern.

### 4. La Sala de l’Isaac: best Wednesday traditional option

> [📍 Map](https://www.google.com/maps/search/La%20Sala%20de%20l%27Isaac%2C%20Llofriu%2C%20Girona%2C%20Spain) · 🚗 15 min from Mas Pastora · 2 min from Mas Oller

La Sala is **closed Tuesday and open Wednesday** according to its live calendar. Lunch runs from 1:00–3:00 p.m., and the restaurant focuses on regional cooking, grilled fish and seafood, and Pals rice.[2]

The ideal Wednesday sequence is a 1:00 lunch, followed by a relaxed transfer or short village stop, then the 5:00 Mas Oller tasting.

### 5. Vicus: best Wednesday food-forward option

> [📍 Map](https://www.google.com/maps/search/Vicus%2C%20Pals%2C%20Girona%2C%20Spain) · 🚗 17 min from Mas Pastora · 4 min from Mas Oller

Vicus does not serve Tuesday lunch but does serve Wednesday lunch from approximately 1:30–3:15. Michelin describes contemporary interpretations of traditional Catalan cooking, seasonal dishes and several rice options designed for sharing.[7]

A 1:30 lunch followed by the 5:00 tasting gives you a comfortable gap. This is the right choice if food quality matters more than rustic atmosphere.

### 6. Candelaria: best Wednesday Peratallada combination

> [📍 Map](https://www.google.com/maps/search/Candelaria%2C%20Carrer%20Major%209%2C%20Peratallada%2C%20Spain) · 🚗 25 min from Mas Pastora · 11 min from Mas Oller

Candelaria’s live calendar marks Tuesday closed and Wednesday open for lunch from 1:00–3:00. It occupies an old stone house in Peratallada and serves creative shared plates in a relaxed setting.[8]

This creates the best Wednesday sightseeing sequence: lunch at 1:00, explore Peratallada until roughly 4:25, then make the 12-minute drive to Mas Oller for the 5:00 tasting.

